  data: {
    LLM: '1. **Bidding**: Each player in turn bids the exact number of tricks they intend to take. 2. **Forced Bid**: The dealer cannot bid an amount that makes the total bids equal to the total available tricks (to ensure someone fails). 3. **Tricks**: Players must follow suit. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest of led suit wins. 4. **Scoring**: Successfully making the bid earns a base bonus (usually 10 points) plus 1 point per trick taken. Any other result scores zero.',
    Player: '1. **Bidding**: Each player in turn bids the exact number of tricks they intend to take. 2. **Forced Bid**: The dealer cannot bid an amount that makes the total bids equal to the total available tricks (to ensure someone fails). 3. **Tricks**: Players must follow suit. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest of led suit wins. 4. **Scoring**: Successfully making the bid earns a base bonus (usually 10 points) plus 1 point per trick taken. Any other result scores zero.',
    objective: 'Score points by winning exactly the number of tricks bid at the start of the round.',
    gameplay: '1. **Bidding**: Each player in turn bids the exact number of tricks they intend to take. 2. **Forced Bid**: The dealer cannot bid an amount that makes the total bids equal to the total available tricks (to ensure someone fails). 3. **Tricks**: Players must follow suit. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest of led suit wins. 4. **Scoring**: Successfully making the bid earns a base bonus (usually 10 points) plus 1 point per trick taken. Any other result scores zero.',
    keyRules: [
      'Must follow suit if possible.',
      'Must hit the bid EXACTLY; taking more or fewer tricks results in a score of zero for the round.',
      'Trump suit is determined by the card turned up from the stock after the deal.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '3 to 7 players playing individually.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card French pack (No Jokers).',
      equipment: 'Standard pack, score pad.',
      dealing: 'The round number (N) determines the hand size. Start at 1 card, increase by 1 each deal to a maximum (e.g., 10), then decrease back to 1. A trump card is turned after each deal.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. **Bidding**: Each player in turn bids the exact number of tricks they intend to take. 2. **Forced Bid**: The dealer cannot bid an amount that makes the total bids equal to the total available tricks (to ensure someone fails). 3. **Tricks**: Players must follow suit. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest of led suit wins. 4. **Scoring**: Successfully making the bid earns a base bonus (usually 10 points) plus 1 point per trick taken. Any other result scores zero.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Boerenbridge is a point-based trick-taking game and does not utilize a monetary or chip-based ante system.',
      deal: 'The initial distribution of N cards per player and the trump card reveal is handled automatically by the system dealer.',
      reveal_market: 'Only the trump-indicator card is public; there is no shared community market of playable cards.',
      buy_market: 'Players cannot purchase or swap cards from any external area; they must succeed using only their dealt hand.',
      buy_stock: 'There is no stock pile to draw from during play; the cards remain out of play after the trump is revealed.',
      fold: 'All players are committed to participating in every trick of the hand to determine if their exact bid was met.',
      check: 'The game uses a trick-taking structure rather than a vying structure where checking would be an appropriate action.',
      call: 'There is no pot to match in this game; competition is based on bidding precision and winning tricks.',
      bet: 'Success is determined by exact trick counts rather than through financial or chip-based betting.',
      raise: 'There are no wagering rounds in Boerenbridge, so the value of the deal cannot be increased via raises.',
      declare: 'Hand resolution is based on objective trick counts rather than a formal declaration phase.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands remain private until individual cards are played into tricks; no full-hand reveal phase occurs.',
      award_pot: 'Winning points are added to a cumulative session total rather than awarded from a physical pot.',
      play_card: 'Must follow suit; highest trump or highest led card wins.',
      draw: 'The complete hand is distributed at the start; no drawing phase exists during the play of the tricks.',
      discard: "Every card in the player's hand must be played into a trick; no cards are discarded or buried.",
      pass: 'Players must bid and play every trick; passing a turn without action is not permitted.',
      bid: "Dealer's bid must not make the total equal to the trick count.",
      meld: 'Boerenbridge is strictly a trick-taking game based on counts rather than forming sequences or melds.',
      go_out: 'The hand terminates only after all available tricks for the current round have been played.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 1 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Score points by winning exactly the number of tricks bid at the start of the round.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. **Bidding**: Each player in turn bids the exact number of tricks they intend to take. 2. **Forced Bid**: The dealer cannot bid an amount that makes the total bids equal to the total available tricks (to ensure someone fails). 3. **Tricks**: Players must follow suit. Highest trump wins; if no trump, highest of led suit wins. 4. **Scoring**: Successfully making the bid earns a base bonus (usually 10 points) plus 1 point per trick taken. Any other result scores zero.',
      'Scoring example: Successful bid = 10 pts + 1 per trick. Unsuccessful = 0 pts. Highest cumulative score after the final round..',
